What:		/proc/sys/kernel/uxio_first_opt
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	OnePlus/Oplus kernel maintainers
Description:
		Global switch for the Oplus UX I/O first request-selection policy.
		The donor default is 1.  Writing 0 leaves requests on the normal
		block dispatch list without applying UX/foreground/background
		priority selection.

What:		/proc/sys/kernel/wbt_enable
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	OnePlus/Oplus kernel maintainers
Description:
		Global switch for block writeback throttling.  The donor default is
		1.  Writing 0 bypasses WBT while preserving its configured latency
		and queue state.

What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/bg_max_depth
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	OnePlus/Oplus kernel maintainers
Description:
		Maximum number of background requests the UX I/O first policy may
		have in flight for a legacy single-queue device.  The default is 24.
		Writes must not exceed the device tag-set maximum depth.

What:		/sys/block/<disk>/queue/ohm_inflight
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	OnePlus/Oplus kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only per-queue request counters.  With UX I/O first enabled the
		output is five newline-separated key/value records in this order:
		async, sync, ux, fg, and bg.
